    {
      "block_id": "1212.0957_p5_b36",
      "text": "The last identity can be viewed as the generalized Stirling transform which\nreduced, for m = 0, to the Stirling transform (1.1) of the sequence an, and\nfor n = 0 reduces to the inverse Stirling transform (1.2) of the sequence bm.\nWe may now formulate the following algorithms\n",
      "bbox": [
        126.72,
        407.38,
        485.34,
        457.17
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        506,
        1629,
        1941,
        1828
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 10.91,
      "font_name": "CMR10",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 275,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "1212.0957_p5_b37",
      "text": "Algorithm 1. Stirling transform\nInput: an\nOutput: bn\nSet Xm = an\u2212m,m\nfor n = 0, 1, . . . do\n",
      "bbox": [
        138.6,
        458.8,
        299.97,
        521.85
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        554,
        1835,
        1199,
        2087
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 10.91,
      "font_name": "CMBX10",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 91,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "1212.0957_p5_b38",
      "text": "Xn := an\nfor m = n, n \u22121, . . . , 0 do\nXm\u22121 := (m \u22121) Xm\u22121 + Xm\nend do\nbn := X0\nend do\n",
      "bbox": [
        138.6,
        523.9,
        298.61,
        599.31
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        554,
        2095,
        1194,
        2397
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 10.91,
      "font_name": "CMMI10",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 86,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "1212.0957_p5_b39",
      "text": "Algorithm 2. inverse Stirling transform\nInput: bm\nOutput: am\nSet Yn = bn,m\u2212n\nfor m = 0, 1, . . . do\n",
      "bbox": [
        138.6,
        611.68,
        336.69,
        674.73
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
